## Statement

Prove that for all real numbers $a,b,c$,
$$a^2+b^2+c^2\ge ab+bc+ca,$$
with equality if and only if $a=b=c$.

## Hint

Look at $(a-b)^2+(b-c)^2+(c-a)^2$.

## Solution

Expanding each square,
$$(a-b)^2+(b-c)^2+(c-a)^2=2\left(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ca\right).$$

A sum of squares is non-negative, so $a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ca\ge0$. It equals $0$ exactly when all three squares are $0$, that is when $a=b=c$.
